# Purpose Section

## Purpose

Defines the Purpose section of the MAM specification. The Purpose section is the only required section of every module and provides a short, clear, and action oriented description of what the module does for its users.

## Inputs

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| content | string | Yes | Full MAM module text that contains the section |
| module | string | No | Module name used in documentation output |

## Outputs

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| purpose | string | Extracted purpose text |
| valid | bool | Whether the section passes validation |
| errors | list | Validation errors found in the section |

## Capabilities

### validate

Checks that the section is present, non empty, and free of code blocks and subsections.

### extract

Pulls the purpose text out of the module body between the heading and the next section.

### document

Renders the purpose text into a documentation fragment.

## Rules

- Every module must have a Purpose section.
- Content must follow the Purpose heading exactly.
- Keep the text clear and concise, ideally one to three sentences.
- Do not place code blocks inside the section.
- Do not use subsections inside the section.
- Start with an action verb that describes the capability.

## Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Content] --> B[Validate]
    B --> C[Extract]
    C --> D[Document]
    D --> E[Output]
```

## Python

```python
def extract_purpose(content: str) -> str:
    purpose = []
    in_purpose = False
    for line in content.split("\n"):
        if line.strip().startswith("## Purpose"):
            in_purpose = True
            continue
        if in_purpose and line.startswith("##"):
            break
        if in_purpose:
            purpose.append(line)
    return "\n".join(purpose).strip()

def validate_purpose(content: str) -> list:
    errors = []
    text = extract_purpose(content)
    if not text:
        errors.append("Missing Purpose section")
        return errors
    if "```" in text:
        errors.append("Purpose contains code blocks")
    if "###" in text:
        errors.append("Purpose contains subsections")
    if text.count(".") < 1:
        errors.append("Purpose is too short")
    return errors

def document_purpose(purpose: str) -> str:
    return "## Module Purpose\n\n" + purpose
```

## Tests

### Input

```yaml
content: |
  ## Purpose

  Validate email addresses using standard RFC checks.
```

### Expected

```yaml
valid: true
errors: []
```

```python
def test_purpose():
    content = "## Purpose\n\nValidate email addresses using standard RFC checks."
    assert extract_purpose(content).startswith("Validate")
    assert validate_purpose(content) == []
    assert "Module Purpose" in document_purpose("hello")
    assert validate_purpose("") == ["Missing Purpose section"]
```

## Examples

### Minimal Purpose

```markdown
## Purpose

Convert XML to JSON format.
```

### Detailed Purpose

```markdown
## Purpose

Manage user authentication and authorization.

This module provides token based authentication with support for multiple providers. It handles registration, login, password reset, and role based access control.
```

